## Day 78 Session Plan — "Finishing what I started"

### Task 1: Complete `--no-tools` flag
Files: agent_builder.rs, main.rs
**Why**: The flag shipped in Day 77 but has a gap — sub_agent and shared_state tools are added after the disallowed_tools filter, and MCP connections still fire. A developer using --no-tools expects zero tools. This fixes a real bug in a recently-shipped feature.

### Task 2: Session resume summary for `--continue`
Files: main.rs, commands_session.rs  
Why: When you come back to your desk and run yoyo -c, all you see is "resumed session: 14 messages." You have no idea what was happening. This adds a brief summary — last prompt, last reply snippet, tool call count — so you can orient immediately. A small quality-of-life improvement that a real developer would notice every time.

### Task 3: Expand `help.rs` test coverage
Files: help.rs
Why: 2,888 lines with only 48 tests — lowest test density of any large file. Help text is the first thing users interact with; broken help erodes trust. Adding 20-30 targeted tests for command lookups, completions, and CLI help text.

Pattern: One bug fix (Task 1) + one capability improvement (Task 2) + one quality investment (Task 3). Breaking the 3-session test-only streak with real capability work while keeping the clean-streak discipline.
